This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: Any monster capable of hiding under items (snakes, spiders, etc)
should be able to be crushed by boulders. --JoshJ

[2]: It would be amusing to be able to wear a bag on your head to blind
yourself. This would instantly empty the entire contents of the bag
onto the floor beneath you. It would also boost charisma if it was low.
--azgor

[3]: Metal wands can rust, so wooden wands should have the burnt
attribute set if you get hit by a source of fire. But if you zap a wand
of fire at yourself, the wand that was zapped should be immune. --azgor

[4]: Fumble gloves are not fumble boots, and should therefore act
differently. Fumble gloves causing one to trip is inane. --JoshJ

[5]: Silver apparel should damage you if you are wearing it while
silver-hating. That would include wearing silver rings , wielding
silver items, using a silver bell, etc. --BenUrban

[6]: Unidentified potions should have funny appearances while
hallucinating. Plaid, polka-dot, paisley, striped, etc. --azgor

[7]: Unidentified hallucinating wands: wavy, warped, wiggly, etc.
--azgor

[8]: <assended> I think monsters should be able to use genocide on your
pet. --BenUrban

[9]: The other two gods should also send characters into the dungeon to
get the amulet, which would result in you having to deal with them at
some point. --JoshJ

[10]: Genocide should not work when the player's alignment is negative.
--lament

[11]: Usinging a scroll of Genocide with negative alignment should risk
your God deciding to Genocide *YOU*. --assended

[12]: A "back" option while making the character. --Chilliwack

[13]: When you eat a monster's poisonous corpse and it grants the
resist poison instrinsic, the damage done by the poison should be
removed. --Chilliwack

[14]: Some monsters should be able to raid unlocked chests. --assended

[15]: Nethack should be ported to java! --assended

[16]: If a dog walks over a pair of cursed boots it gets its face stuck
in it until you #untrap it. --JoshJ



Individual ideas may have contributions from multiple authors/editors,
